    "source": "\n**Location:** `curt-home-office`\n\n**Frame:** The critique window from [page 039](039.md) reopens at the edge of the map, byline and date visible, scrolled to its own thesis.\n\n**Screen / system text — PUBLISHED CRITIQUE (PAGE 039, 3 SEPTEMBER 2026) (PARAPHRASED):**\n`THERE WERE NEVER THREE CIVILIZATIONS. THERE WAS A PERSISTENCE OF CONTEXT ACROSS THE WHOLE PERIOD.`\n\n**Dialogue — CURT:**\n> He said that the day before this report came out. He was arguing about the Artifactory record. His post did not discuss this lane.\n\n**Provenance:** `documented` + `reconstructed` — `IOB-CIV`, attributed paraphrase of the post's persistence-of-context claim; the post is dated 3 September and does not mention the wiki. Curt's line is reconstruction. The critic is not credited with anticipating the concurrency finding: persistence of context and overlapping populations are different claims, and the page must keep them apart.\n\n",
    "title": "The dated critique returns beside the map"
  }
